## Problem

`v0.1.0-rc.4` is still unpublished after both the VERSION merge and the first publication-flow retry. The release workflow used one concurrency group for every `main` run (`release-refs/heads/main`) with `cancel-in-progress: false`, so a stalled/queued older release can block later retries indefinitely.

## Change

- remove the shared `main` concurrency lock;
- add `workflow_dispatch` as the conventional explicit retry path;
- add a 15-minute timeout to Windows build/package and 5-minute timeout to Linux publish;
- retain the self-change trigger so merging this PR automatically retries the current unpublished `VERSION=0.1.0-rc.4`;
- keep publication idempotent: an existing Release is never overwritten.

No mod/runtime code changes.

